  "caption": "Quinn's late-night \"one more episode\" habit came with a sleepy little finger, and then a very unfunny bump to the funny bone.\n\nTingling in the little finger and half the ring finger often comes from the ulnar nerve being squeezed or stretched at the elbow. Long periods with the elbow bent, like phone calls, folded arms, leaning on elbows, cycling or sleeping curled up, can add up.\n\nWhat often helps: keeping the elbow straighter at night (a loosely wrapped towel or soft splint), using a headset, unfolding your arms, taking micro-breaks, gentle nerve glides within comfort, and general arm and shoulder strength. Pressing on it or aggressive stretching tends to backfire.\n\nConstant numbness, grip weakness, clumsiness or thinning hand muscles are worth a GP assessment.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
